{%- comment -%}
  The three seals, moved out of the hero.

  They used to sit inside lada-hero, stacked under the CTAs and on top
  of the photograph — so the one thing the page has to prove was
  competing with the one photograph the label owns, and losing. The
  spec's call is to rehouse them in a band of their own directly under
  the plate, where the hero's 66svh clamp leaves the top edge of this
  band visible above the fold.

  Drawn in lines and type only: no icons, no boxes, no shadows, no
  fill beyond the panel ground. That is khaadi's PDP rule — the
  information architecture is drawn entirely with lines — and it is
  what keeps three claims from reading as three marketing tiles.
{%- endcomment -%}
<section class="lada lada__proof" id="lada-proof">
  <div class="lada__wrap">
    <dl class="lada__proof-list">
      {%- for i in (1..3) -%}
        {%- liquid
          case i
            when 1
              assign t = section.settings.seal1_title | default: 'Cut in-house'
              assign d = section.settings.seal1_text | default: 'Cut in our own workshop in Sheikhupura.'
            when 2
              assign t = section.settings.seal2_title | default: 'Unconditional guarantee'
              assign d = section.settings.seal2_text | default: 'Replaced or refunded, no conditions, no time limit.'
            when 3
              assign t = section.settings.seal3_title | default: 'Cut to measure'
              assign d = section.settings.seal3_text | default: '38R to 46R as standard, measured in the shop at no charge.'
          endcase
        -%}
        <div class="lada__proof-item"><dt>{{ t }}</dt><dd>{{ d }}</dd></div>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Lada proof",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Three claims, directly under the hero. Drawn in lines and type — no icons." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal1_title", "label": "Seal 1 title" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal1_text", "label": "Seal 1 text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal2_title", "label": "Seal 2 title" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal2_text", "label": "Seal 2 text" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal3_title", "label": "Seal 3 title" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "seal3_text", "label": "Seal 3 text" }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Lada proof" }]
}
{% endschema %}
